mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# Fintech Rewards & Membership API\n\n## Purpose\nBackend for an Indian fintech rewards and membership platform. Users register, buy one of seven fixed membership plans via manual UPI payment, earn referral rewards, hold a wallet ledger, request withdrawals, receive notifications, and open support tickets. Admins verify payments, approve withdrawals and referral rewards, manage plans and settings, and export reports.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n- Identity is the caller's Internet Computer principal. There are no passwords or sessions in the canister.\n- The frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- Registration is a prerequisite for most endpoints. A direct API caller must first call `_initialize_access_control()` once as a signed-in (non-anonymous) caller to register its principal with the access-control system. The first caller to do so receives the `#admin` role; every later caller receives `#user`. After that, call `registerUser` once to create the profile. A caller that never registered is unregistered even if it belongs to the app owner, and a principal derived against a different derivation origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n- Anonymous callers and unregistered principals are rejected on guarded endpoints. An unregistered caller traps with `User is not registered` (from `getUserRole`); wallet, referral, withdrawal, notification and support endpoints trap with `Unauthorized: Only registered users ...`. Admin endpoints return empty results or `null` for non-admins.\n\n## Units and encoding\n- Timestamps are signed nanoseconds since the Unix epoch (`Time.now()`), encoded as Candid `int`.\n- Amounts are whole Indian rupees, encoded as Candid `nat`.\n- Identifiers are `nat` counters.\n- Principals are Candid `principal`; in OQL rows they appear as text.\n- File references (profile picture, payment screenshot, QR image) are object-storage `ExternalBlob` values.\n- Variants: payment status `#pending|#approved|#rejected`; withdrawal status `#pending|#approved|#rejected|#completed`; transaction kind `#credit|#debit`; transaction type `#payment|#reward|#referral|#withdrawal`; transaction status `#pending|#completed|#failed`; referral status `#pending|#eligible|#rewarded|#rejected`; withdrawal method `#upi|#bank`; ticket status `#open|#inProgress|#resolved|#closed`.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n- Payment: `submitPayment` creates a `#pending` submission. An admin calls `adminApprovePayment` or `adminRejectPayment`. Approval activates a 30-day membership, records a wallet debit, and notifies the user. Poll `listMyPayments` for status.\n- Withdrawal: `requestUpiWithdrawal` / `requestBankWithdrawal` create a `#pending` request and reserve a pending wallet debit. Admin `adminApproveWithdrawal`, `adminRejectWithdrawal`, then `adminMarkWithdrawalPaid`. Poll `listMyWithdrawals`.\n- Referral: a referral starts `#pending`; `adminApprovePayment` marks the buyer's pending referral `#eligible`; `adminApproveReferralReward` credits the referrer and marks it `#rewarded`.\n- Notifications: poll `listMyNotifications` and `getUnreadNotificationCount`; mark read with `markNotificationRead` / `markAllNotificationsRead`.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n- `submitPayment` rejects a duplicate UTR across all submissions, so retrying the same UTR returns `#err`.\n- `adminApprovePayment` and `adminRejectPayment` are idempotent for non-pending payments: they return the current view without re-activating or re-crediting.\n- `adminApproveReferralReward` only credits a referral in `#eligible` state; other states return `null`.\n- `markNotificationRead` is scoped to the caller and returns `false` for another user's notification.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n- `registerUser` returns `#err` for a duplicate email or mobile, an invalid referral code, or self-referral.\n- Wallet balances are derived from the ledger; they are never set directly.\n- Withdrawals are limited to the withdrawable balance and the admin-configured minimum.\n- `getAdminSettings` is public; admin mutations require the `#admin` role.\n- OQL `schema()` and `execute()` are exposed for the Data Intelligence agent; each table enforces its own authorization level."
  };
};
